# Dev Notes 52 — Runtime Native Worker Backend Execution Integration v1

**Date:** 2026-06-19  
**Branch:** `runtime-native-worker-backend-execution-integration-v1`  
**Status:** Staged candidate from uploaded `main` mirror and plan/spec; assistant sandbox syntax checks, fixture coverage, worker import hygiene, targeted nativeWorkerBackend execution integration smoke, current contract-chain smokes, and broader mock/static lifecycle/worker regression smokes passed. Real-runtime testing by Michael, artifact/package guard, direct GitHub branch inspection, and post-merge `main` inspection remain incomplete gates before merge readiness.

---

## 1. Purpose

This branch wires the first real native text-generation execution path from the accepted execute-action descriptor chain into the existing Runtime Dev native runtime path.

The branch adds a narrow behavior seam:

```text
action/orchestration contract chain
  -> execute-action behavior seam
  -> executable nativeWorkerBackend adapter
  -> existing parent runtime substrate
  -> scheduler / request lifecycle / settlement / stream / lifecycle coordinators
  -> workerBridge
  -> llama_worker
  -> real model output
  -> result/event outcome mapping
```

The branch does not create a second native execution path and does not let backend adapters call `workerBridge` or `llama_worker` directly.

---

## 2. Source-truth notes

Source truth for the branch remains GitHub `main` unless Michael explicitly promotes an uploaded artifact.

This staged candidate was prepared from the uploaded `runtime-dev-repo-main.zip` mirror after a minimal GitHub source-shape refresh showed the expected current layout and latest merge posture.

Known caveat: raw GitHub retrieval may display some files as line-collapsed. Treat that as a retrieval/display artifact unless direct file-page inspection or a local clone confirms source formatting damage.

---

## 3. Architecture decision

The previous runtime work is split into two classifications in the new stack:

```text
Existing native model machinery
  -> first concrete replaceable backend family: nativeWorkerBackend

Existing parent-side scheduler/request/settlement/stream/lifecycle machinery
  -> shared Runtime Dev execution substrate
```

This branch makes `nativeWorkerBackend` executable for the accepted `text.generate` route while preserving scheduler, request lifecycle, settlement, stream shaping, lifecycle, `workerBridge`, and worker ownership in the parent/native runtime substrate.

