## 14. Caveats / known risks

Finding: public API changed.  
Affected surface: `runtime.mjs`, public-entrypoint guard.  
Why it matters: prior contract-only branches intentionally rejected `executeAction` exposure. This branch intentionally adds only narrow `executeAction(orchestrationDescriptor)`.  
Smallest safe correction: keep the input limited to accepted orchestration descriptors and defer raw action-envelope dispatch.  
What still needs verification: direct GitHub branch inspection and Michael real-runtime execution.

Finding: fixture manifest grew from runtime reachability.  
Affected surface: fixture-copy tests.  
Why it matters: `runtime.mjs` now imports the execute-action seam, which makes contract modules reachable in runtime fixtures.  
Smallest safe correction: update `tests/helpers/runtimeFixtureFiles.mjs`; `checkRuntimeFixtureCoverage.mjs` passed with 85 files.  
What still needs verification: package extraction/recheck after candidate ZIP generation.

Finding: real execution behavior is only mock-smoke-tested in sandbox.  
Affected surface: native/model behavior.  
Why it matters: sandbox mock tests do not prove local node-llama-cpp/model execution.  
Smallest safe correction: Michael local `REAL_RUNTIME=1` smoke before merge readiness.  
What still needs verification: non-empty real result, streaming handle behavior, cancellation mapping, prompt compatibility after executeAction.

